1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Nature data has blind spots.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
WildGap finds where one more hour of looking could be useful.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Search any location. Choose a 2, 5, or 10 kilometre area.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Comparable H3 cells reveal uneven GBIF observation coverage.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Latest 12 completed months vs. the preceding 36-month baseline.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,500
Low records are not a wildlife decline. They are a reason to look again.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:33,000
55% density gap + 30% coverage change + 15% target gap.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
When evidence is too thin, WildGap suppresses the ranking.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Open-Meteo adds climate context and seven-day field conditions.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Weather changes timing—not the biodiversity score.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Generate a printable, safe, 60-minute mission.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
No sign-in. Missions stay on-device and travel in validated links.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
A clearly labeled Winnipeg demo keeps judging outage-safe.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,500
Deployed product and technical verification—no field or tester claim.

15
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
Find where nature data is missing, then go look.
